# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which checks files
# out with CRLF line endings. A CRLF on a shebang line makes the Linux kernel
# look for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", and the container exits
# at startup with a bewildering "no such file or directory" naming a file that
# plainly exists. Pin everything that runs inside the image to LF.
#
# After adding this file, run `git add --renormalize .` once to rewrite any
# already-committed CRLF blobs.

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
docker/** text eol=lf
bin/console text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch these.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.epub binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
